This package ports the inference pipeline of homr (https://github.com/liebharc/homr,
AGPL-3.0, Copyright the homr authors) to run homr's published ONNX weights in the
browser via onnxruntime-web (WebGPU for SegNet and the encoder, WASM for the
decoder). Python homr is used only as the model exporter and correctness oracle;
no Python runs in the browser.

homr builds on prior work by its authors and the community. In particular this
package acknowledges:

- homr — https://github.com/liebharc/homr (AGPL-3.0)
- oemer — https://github.com/Britness/oemer (the end-to-end OMR approach homr's
  segmentation pipeline follows)
- Polyphonic-TrOMR — https://github.com/bernardosda/Polyphonic-TrOMR (the
  transformer architecture homr's encoder/decoder derive from)

The pre-trained ONNX weights are downloaded from homr's public release
(https://github.com/liebharc/homr/releases/tag/onnx_checkpoints) and are used
under the terms published there by the homr authors.

The gbk audio engine that consumes this package's MIDI output is a separate
work and is not covered by this license.
